# The external binaries of a release build; never committed. Without the config that names them no
# build needs this folder, so the gates pass on a clean checkout.
#
# `anima` (INS-002): the builder's bundle step (src/builder/sidecar.rs) builds it from the job's
# commit with ANIMA_VERSION, puts `binaries/anima-<target-triple>` here (and, on macOS,
# `anima-universal-apple-darwin` made with lipo), and passes `bundle.externalBin: ["binaries/anima"]`
# in `--config` to `tauri build` and `tauri bundle`.
#
# The agent sidecar (MET-019, D-10 d). The release build must:
#   1. build `anima-agent` for the app's target triple from the same commit;
#   2. place it at `binaries/anima-agent-<target-triple>` (this folder);
#   3. pass `--config tauri.release.conf.json` to `tauri build`, which names it in `bundle.externalBin`.
/binaries/
